function sources(){openUtility('Sources & map notes',`<p>Explore the Northwest using public agency data and original Outzide destination information. Community actions use your Zaylist account.</p><h3>Places & conditions</h3><p>Destination data was captured from Zaylist on ${stamp(metadata.fetchedAt)}. Conditions cards retain source names and observation dates. Forecasts can refresh directly from the National Weather Service.</p><p>${link('https://www.zaylist.com/outz','Current Outzide')}&nbsp; ${link('https://www.weather.gov','National Weather Service')}</p><h3>Geographically anchored routes</h3><p>Trails use Forest Service line geometry captured ${stamp(metadata.routeFetchedAt)}. A cyan trace shows the mapped route, not a decorative drawing. Unverified nearby routes are not attached to destination cards. The route distance describes mapped segments, not a recommended itinerary or guaranteed round trip.</p><p>${link(metadata.routeSource,'USFS trail geometry')}</p><p>${link('https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright','OpenStreetMap trail data')} · ${link('https://mapterhorn.com/attribution/','Elevation sources')}</p><h3>Map & artwork</h3><p>The original Mapz surface renderer uses OpenFreeMap vector tiles, OpenMapTiles and OpenStreetMap data. Terrain and contours use Mapterhorn elevation tiles at 1× vertical scale. Heights are terrain-model estimates, not surveyed trail measurements. OpenStreetMap footpaths remain visible at trail zoom levels. Place motifs and Outzide wordmark are the existing Zaylist assets. Hologram light materials reuse the events map renderer.</p><p>Private stays retain public town/region coordinates only; places without published coordinates remain in the list.</p>`)}
